  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity Support for sustainable energy use through capital investments that improve access to clean energy and support refugees and communities around the Dadaab and Kakuma refugee camps cope with the effects of Climate Change. is a component of Support for Protection and Assistance of Refugees in Kenya (SPARK)  reported by FCDO with a funding type of 109 - Multilateral organisation and a budget of &#xa3;1,700,000. It works in the following sector(s): Environmental policy and administrative management.</narrative>
  </description>
